- [(3) Law of Segregation or Law of Purity of Gametes]{color=gray}
  - [In sexual reproduction, each parent contributes just one of their alleles to its offspring]{color=gray}
- [(4) Law of Independent Assortment]{color=gray}
  - [different pairs of alleles are passed onto the offspring independently of each other.]{color=gray}
  - [inheritance of genes at one location does not influence the inheritance of genes at another location.]{color=gray}

=== layout: two-panels

# Dominance

@left

- In each genotype there is a dominant allele, the phenotype is determined by dominant allele
- Since purple is more common than [white]{color=gray}, purple is likely dominant to [white]{color=gray}

@right

![Slide image 6](assets/lect04c-two_principles/image_006.png)

